==== Important note regarding installation ====

If the OEM firmware has been upgraded an odd number of times (i.e. 1, 3, 5, 7 etc.) , the install **will fail**. If in doubt, follow the workaround below:
 
  * Download the "Firmware OpenWrt Install" image from the table above.
  * Use the web interface of the original OEM software:
    - Navigate to: "Maintenance" -> "Diagnostics" -> "Diagnostics" -> "Collect Now" -> "Download".
    - Extract the ''debug/diag_zysh_system/diag_zysh_system.dbg'' file from the resulting debug tar.bz2 archive.
    - ''grep -i image debug/diag_zysh_system/diag_zysh_system.dbg''.
    - Ensure ''Current Image num'' is **1**.
    - If not, then flash a Zyxel OEM firmware upgrade (**not** an OpenWrt install image), and re-check.
  * Once you are sure that the Install the ''Current Image num'' is **1**, then install the OpenWrt "factory" image via: "Maintenance" -> "Firmware Package".

According to the OpenWrt issue tracked in [[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/14566]], OpenWRT can only be installed to the first firmware slot of the router's dual-boot configuration (referred to alternately as Slot 0, Slot A in the issue), therefore there is unlikely to be a workaround -- addressing this would require building an installer which handles the above steps for the user.

